        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: enforce W&B sandbox ownership",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- require W&B existing-sandbox run, status, and stop operations to prove membership in provider inventory tagged `crabbox`\n- fail closed before Exec, Get, or Stop when tagged inventory is unavailable or does not contain the requested ID\n- document the ownership boundary and why `--reclaim` remains unsupported\n\nCloses https://github.com/openclaw/crabbox/issues/786\n\n## Verification\n\nCurrent candidate: `ed1db34bc7132bd174035e25d14f54a9441ca2bc`\n\nLocal validation on the current candidate:\n\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD`\n- `go test -race ./internal/providers/wandb`\n- `go vet ./internal/providers/wandb`\n- `go vet ./...`\n- `scripts/check-docs.sh`\n\nHosted checks are re-running after the rebase onto `origin/main` (`a140db6303d4fed0e624f0747c30cb5a072409fa`).\n\n## Pre-merge live gate\n\nBlocked pending W&B/CoreWeave credentials: this shell has no `WANDB_API_KEY`, `CRABBOX_WANDB_API_KEY`, `COREWEAVE_API_KEY`, or `CRABBOX_COREWEAVE_API_KEY`. This PR must remain unmerged until authenticated exact-head proof shows: tagged owned sandbox existing-ID run/status/stop succeeds, a Crabbox-labelled but unowned sandbox is denied, and cleanup leaves zero residue.\n\n## Security / configuration\n\nNo new credential or configuration requirement. Raw W&B sandbox IDs are now accepted for mutable or command-execution operations only when the provider-side `crabbox` ownership tag is present.",
